From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add riscv64 to the binary-path platform tables

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: pyscn has no riscv64 CI runner, so a drive-by PR could not be exercised by upstream's own release workflow; needs a maintainer discussion first]

python/src/pyscn/main.py's get_binary_path() and
python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py's get_mcp_binary_path() each normalize
platform.machine() to "amd64"/"arm64" and raise FileNotFoundError for
anything else, then build the bundled binary's filename as
pyscn-{system}-{machine} / pyscn-mcp-{system}-{machine}. They only
know the two architectures upstream's own python-release.yml build
matrix covers (linux-amd64, linux-arm64, windows-amd64, darwin-arm64);
on riscv64 they refuse to even look for a binary, let alone find the
ones this port's build-pyscn.yml stages at
pyscn/bin/pyscn-linux-riscv64 and pyscn/bin/pyscn-mcp-linux-riscv64
(built by python/scripts/build_platform_wheel.sh linux-riscv64 ...).

Add machine in ('riscv64',) -> 'riscv64' to both, matching
platform.machine() reporting "riscv64" verbatim on that architecture
and the GOOS=linux GOARCH=riscv64 naming build_platform_wheel.sh
already uses for every other platform. Existing platforms resolve
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/src/pyscn/main.py     | 2 ++
 python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/python/src/pyscn/main.py b/python/src/pyscn/main.py
index 382f23c..75aa850 100644
--- a/python/src/pyscn/main.py
+++ b/python/src/pyscn/main.py
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@ def get_binary_path() -> str:
         machine = 'amd64'
     elif machine in ('aarch64', 'arm64'):
         machine = 'arm64'
+    elif machine in ('riscv64',):
+        machine = 'riscv64'
     else:
         raise FileNotFoundError(
             f"Unsupported architecture: {machine}. "
diff --git a/python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py b/python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py
index 9f0b574..571a4e3 100644
--- a/python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py
+++ b/python/src/pyscn/mcp_main.py
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ def get_mcp_binary_path() -> str:
         machine = 'amd64'
     elif machine in ('aarch64', 'arm64'):
         machine = 'arm64'
+    elif machine in ('riscv64',):
+        machine = 'riscv64'
     else:
         raise FileNotFoundError(
             f"Unsupported architecture: {machine}. "
